    "stop_reason": "success",
    "result_text": "All changes compile and the test suite is green (`Tests run: 1, Failures: 0, Errors: 0` \u2192 `BUILD SUCCESS`).\n\n## Summary\n\nThe `householdId` is now deterministic from `(normalizedLastName, postcode)`, and everything keyed off the household uses that computed id. Changes were kept as small, cohesive edits in low-complexity util/support classes so the large controller barely moved.\n\n- **`util/Household.java`** \u2014 `idFor` now takes an `Owner` and hashes `normalizedLastName + '|' + postcode` (was `lastName|address`). Single source of truth for the id; still 12 upper-case hex chars of SHA-256.\n- **`mapper/OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 one expression updated to `Household.idFor(owner)`.\n- **`util/GoldTier.java`** \u2014 household-size check routed through the computed id (`Household.idFor(owner)` / `idFor(o)`).\n- **`rest/advice/DuplicateHouseholdException.java`** \u2014 `rejectIfDuplicate` now detects duplicates by comparing computed `householdId` (same last name + postcode), still bypassed by `sharesHousehold`. Dropped the now-dead local normalization.\n- **`util/PossibleDuplicate.java`** \u2014 `assign` takes `sharesHousehold`; a declared household member is never flagged as a suspected duplicate.\n- **`rest/controller/v1/OwnerRestControllerV1.java`** \u2014 reads `sharesHousehold` once, adds the household-duplicate rejection (409 unless the flag is set), and passes the flag to `PossibleDuplicate.assign`.\n\nBehavior now matches the spec: two owners with the same last name and postcode share a `householdId` automatically; a second such owner is a 409 household duplicate unless it sets `sharesHousehold`, in which case it's created as a declared member and not marked a possible duplicate.",
